summary:
  A parked station's writer runs on however long the pause lasts.

history:
  Until 2026.44 a pause cost the line one window: the single file's
  writer ended at its cap. The segment writer has none, so a pause somebody
  forgot went on fetching the station until Stop, and after one window the
  paused place was pushed out of the folder all the same. The capture ends
  thirty seconds before the place would leave: measured on the rig with a
  window of two minutes, no curl and no ffmpeg from 90 s after the pause on
  and a folder that stood still.

target:
  package/contents/ui/TimeshiftEngine.qml

find:
          if (slide && writerUp && !shifted && _stage === "" && SlideLogic.parkEndsCapture(shiftPosMs, runMs, keepMs)) _endCapture();

replace:
          if (false) _endCapture();

expect:
  Killed by tests/qml/tst_slideengine.qml::test_a_pause_that_reaches_the_windows_edge_ends_the_capture_and_keeps_what_was_cut.
